===== Aggregate functions in HAVING are supported =====
Query parse tree:
SELECT
  Out_0:`a`
   = C0:`a`
  Out_1:`count(*)`
   = A0:Count(1)
FROM tbl
GROUP BY
  C0:`a`

Aggregation program (4 instructions):
Instr. DEST SRC DESCRIPTION
LoadI  r00  I00 r00 = I00:1
Count  A00  r00 A00:COUNT <- r00:1
Load   r00  C01 r00 = C01:`b`
Sum    A01  r00 A01:SUM <- r00:`b`

No NDB connection, so no index scan analysis.

Output in mysql-style tab separated format.
The program for post-processing and output has 9 instructions.

===== GROUP BY column in HAVING =====
HAVING can only reference aggregate functions, such as COUNT(*) or SUM(col), and constants; 'a' is not an aggregate. Filter GROUP BY columns in WHERE, and repeat an aggregate instead of using its output alias.
Error handling: RPE
